<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chen Yonghua</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1634–1680</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chen Yonghua was the chief minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-jing">Zheng Jing</a>, ruler of the Kingdom of Tungning on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a>. He organised a Chinese-style administration, settled soldiers on farmland and promoted salt-making and trade. In 1666 he founded Taiwan's first Confucian temple and school in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tainan">Tainan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chen-yonghua.jpg" alt="Chen Yonghua" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pbdragonwang · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E9%99%B3%E6%B0%B8%E8%8F%AF%E7%A5%9E%E5%83%8F.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
